.TH OQ 1 "2026" "oq" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oq \- address nodes in an OpenAPI document
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oq
.I command
.I spec
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oq
resolves addresses in an OpenAPI (YAML or JSON) document and acts on the text at them: list what is there and how big it is, print it exactly, map a line back to a node, find references, or replace a node.
.I spec
is a file, or
.B \-
for standard input.
Searching, linting, formatting and bundling are left to other tools.
.PP
Listings are one record per line, tab separated. Raw output is the node's source text. Success is silent, errors go to standard error.
.SH ADDRESSES
.TP
.B /components/schemas/item
JSON pointer (also
.BR #/... ).
.TP
.B schemas/item.yaml#/Item
Pointer into an external file, relative to the spec's directory.
.TP
.B GET /items/{item_id}
Operation by method and path.
.TP
.B path:/items/{item_id}
The whole path item, with all its methods.
.TP
.B opid:listItems
Operation by operationId.
.TP
.B schema:item
Named schema.
.PP
Addresses printed by
.B oq
are JSON pointers without spaces; special characters are percent-encoded.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B outline \fIspec\fR [\fIaddr\fR] [\-\-depth N]
Child addresses with kind, approximate tokens, line range and anchor note.
.TP
.B ls \fIspec\fR ops|schemas|tags|files
One entry per line with approximate tokens.
.TP
.B get \fIspec\fR \fIaddr\fR [\-\-metadata]
Print the node's source text. \fB\-o json\fR converts the node to JSON; \fB\-o yaml\fR is the same as the default. With
.BR \-\-metadata ,
print address, kind, range, hash and token count instead, in the \fB\-o\fR format (a tab separated row by default).
.TP
.B at \fIspec\fR \fIline\fR[:\fIcol\fR]
Address of the innermost node at that position.
.TP
.B deps \fIspec\fR \fIaddr\fR [\-\-depth N] [\-\-unresolved]
Nodes referenced by
.IR addr ,
breadth first. Default depth 1.
.TP
.B refs \fIspec\fR \fIaddr\fR
Nodes that reference
.IR addr .
.TP
.B set \fIspec\fR \fIaddr\fR [\-\-expect H] [\-i] [\-\-file F]
Replace the value at
.I addr
with the YAML or JSON read from standard input.
.TP
.B insert \fIspec\fR \fIaddr\fR [\-\-after KEY] [\-\-expect H] [\-i] [\-\-file F]
Add the entries of the input mapping or sequence to the container at
.IR addr .
.TP
.B rm \fIspec\fR \fIaddr\fR [\-\-expect H] [\-i]
Remove the entry at
.IR addr .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output tsv|name|columns=a,b|json|yaml
Output format (default tsv; there is no \-\-json flag). name prints only the first column; columns= selects columns by name. json and yaml repeat field names on every record and cost more tokens. For write commands only with \-i.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-tokens N
Output cap in approximate tokens (default 5000, 0 disables). Over the cap nothing is printed, a narrower command is suggested and the exit status is 4.
.TP
.B \-\-header
Print column names as the first line of a listing (outline, ls, deps, refs).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help for the command.
.TP
.B \-i
Edit the file in place, atomically, under a directory lock. The edit is re-applied, including the hash check, if the file changed meanwhile.
.TP
.B \-\-expect H
Hash from
.B get \-o columns=hash
(at least 6 hex characters). Mismatch exits with 3.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
ok
.TP
.B 1
address not found
.TP
.B 2
usage or parse error
.TP
.B 3
stale write
.TP
.B 4
output over the size cap
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
grep \-n 'deprecated: true' openapi.yaml | cut \-d: \-f1 | xargs \-n1 oq at openapi.yaml
oq deps openapi.yaml 'GET /items/{item_id}' \-o name | xargs \-I% oq get openapi.yaml %
h=$(oq get openapi.yaml schema:item \-o columns=hash)
oq set openapi.yaml schema:item \-\-expect "$h" \-i < item.yaml
.fi
